IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja2-part5-ca-criminal`

-- Tests for ss 60D and 60E. Expected values are written from the text of the sections, not from the code.

-- s 60D: the seven matters of paragraphs (a) to (g), and nothing else
#ASSERT (`s 60D the matter is one of the matters of the criminal jurisdiction of the Court of Appeal` `s 60D(a) an appeal against a decision made by the General Division in the exercise of its original criminal jurisdiction`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60D the matter is one of the matters of the criminal jurisdiction of the Court of Appeal` `s 60D(b) a petition for confirmation under Division 1A of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60D the matter is one of the matters of the criminal jurisdiction of the Court of Appeal` `s 60D(c) a review of a decision of the Court of Appeal, or a decision of the General Division, under Division 1B of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60D the matter is one of the matters of the criminal jurisdiction of the Court of Appeal` `s 60D(d) a case stated to the Court of Appeal under section 395 or 396 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60D the matter is one of the matters of the criminal jurisdiction of the Court of Appeal` `s 60D(e) a reference to the Court of Appeal under section 397 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60D the matter is one of the matters of the criminal jurisdiction of the Court of Appeal` `s 60D(f) a motion to the Court of Appeal under Division 5 of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60D the matter is one of the matters of the criminal jurisdiction of the Court of Appeal` `s 60D(g) a reference to the Court of Appeal under section 18 of the Extradition Act 1968`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60D the matter is one of the matters of the criminal jurisdiction of the Court of Appeal` `s 60D another kind of matter`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 60E(1): "if the Tenth Schedule so provides, be heard and determined by a single Judge"
#ASSERT (`s 60E(1) the case may be heard and determined by that number of Judges despite section 50(1)` 1 (JUST TRUE) (JUST `a single Judge`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60E(1) the case may be heard and determined by that number of Judges despite section 50(1)` 2 (JUST TRUE) (JUST `a single Judge`)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60E(1) the case may be heard and determined by that number of Judges despite section 50(1)` 1 (JUST TRUE) (JUST `2 Judges`)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60E(1) the case may be heard and determined by that number of Judges despite section 50(1)` 1 (JUST TRUE) (JUST `a single Judge or 2 Judges`)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60E(1) the case may be heard and determined by that number of Judges despite section 50(1)` 1 (JUST TRUE) NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the Tenth Schedule does not allow a single Judge in this kind of case: the "if" is not met
#ASSERT (`s 60E(1) the case may be heard and determined by that number of Judges despite section 50(1)` 1 (JUST FALSE) (JUST `a single Judge`)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60E(1) the case may be heard and determined by that number of Judges despite section 50(1)` 2 (JUST FALSE) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- whether the Tenth Schedule allows a single Judge is not answered: the answer is NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60E(1) the case may be heard and determined by that number of Judges despite section 50(1)` 1 NOTHING (JUST `a single Judge`)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60E(1) the case may be heard and determined by that number of Judges despite section 50(1)` 2 NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 60E(2): "A Judge must not sit in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide any of the following matters, or any matter related"
#ASSERT (`s 60E(2) the Judge may sit in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide the matter` `s 60E(2)(a) an appeal against a conviction before the Judge or a sentence passed by the Judge`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60E(2) the Judge may sit in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide the matter` `s 60E(2)(b) a petition for confirmation under Division 1A of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 lodged in respect of a sentence of death passed by the Judge on an accused`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60E(2) the Judge may sit in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide the matter` `s 60E(2)(c) a case stated by the Judge under section 395 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60E(2) the Judge may sit in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide the matter` `s 60E(2)(d) a reference under section 397 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 of a question of law of public interest that has arisen in a criminal matter determined by the Judge`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60E(2) the Judge may sit in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide the matter` `s 60E(2) a matter related to a matter in paragraphs (a) to (d)`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60E(2) the Judge may sit in the Court of Appeal to hear or decide the matter` `s 60E(2) another matter`) EQUALS NOTHING
